## 1. Original Authorship Must Be Preserved

SniffRTP was originally created by:

(deepslate/sniff/sussy)**imsoback**

No person, company, organization, developer, distributor, fork maintainer, marketplace seller, server operator, or other party may claim, imply, advertise, represent, or suggest that they created the original SniffRTP project.

You may identify yourself as the author of your own modifications only.

You may not replace the original author's name with your own name.

You may not describe a fork or modified copy as an entirely original project if it contains SniffRTP source code or substantial portions of SniffRTP.

## 2. Mandatory Credit Line

Every copy of SniffRTP, including modified versions and derivative works containing SniffRTP code, must preserve the following line exactly:

# Licensed as (deepslate/sniff/sussy)**imsoback**'s SniffRTP

This line:

* must not be deleted;
* must not be edited;
* must not be shortened;
* must not be renamed;
* must not be commented out differently for the purpose of hiding it;
* must not be encoded or obfuscated to make it difficult to read;
* must not be moved into an inaccessible location solely to hide attribution;
* must not be replaced with another person's credit;
* must remain plainly readable by a normal user inspecting the configuration file.

When `config.yml` exists, this line must appear in `config.yml`.

Additional credits may be added, but they must not replace, obscure, contradict, or reduce the visibility of the original credit.

## 3. License File Must Remain

Every redistributed copy of SniffRTP or derivative work containing SniffRTP code must include an unmodified copy of this License.

The `LICENSE` file may not be removed, renamed for the purpose of concealment, replaced with another license, or modified.

Additional licenses covering separately written code may be included only if they do not conflict with this License.

## 4. Same-License Requirement

Any redistributed modified version, fork, port, derivative work, or project containing substantial SniffRTP code must continue to distribute the SniffRTP-derived portions under this License.

You may not redistribute SniffRTP-derived code under terms that remove or weaken the attribution and preservation requirements contained in this License.

You may not sublicense the original SniffRTP code under a license that permits removal of the required attribution.

## 5. Modified Versions Must Be Clearly Identified

If you modify SniffRTP and distribute the modified version, you must clearly state that the version has been modified.

A modified version must not be represented as an official release created by the original author.

Where reasonably practical, redistributed modified versions must contain a notice similar to:

Modified version of SniffRTP.
Original author: (deepslate/sniff/sussy)**imsoback**
Modifications by: <modifier name>

The modifier may identify their own contributions, but the original attribution must remain present.

## 6. No False Ownership Claims

You may not:

* claim ownership of the original SniffRTP project;
* claim that you wrote original SniffRTP code that you did not write;
* remove original authorship information;
* replace original authorship information with your own;
* falsely register the original SniffRTP project as your own work;
* falsely claim exclusive authorship over SniffRTP-derived code;
* intentionally conceal that a redistributed project contains SniffRTP code;
* market a substantially unchanged copy of SniffRTP as an independently created plugin.

Forking, modifying, improving, translating, porting, optimizing, maintaining, or commercially distributing SniffRTP does not make the distributor the original author of SniffRTP.

## 7. Renaming Does Not Remove Attribution Requirements

You may rename a modified fork or derivative work.

However, renaming SniffRTP does not remove any obligation under this License.

A renamed project containing SniffRTP code must still:

* credit the original SniffRTP author;
* preserve this License;
* preserve the required attribution line;
* identify itself as derived from or based on SniffRTP where reasonably visible.

Changing the project name does not permit you to claim original authorship.

## 8. Source-Code Attribution

Where SniffRTP source files contain copyright, author, attribution, or licensing notices, those notices must remain intact.

You may not deliberately remove authorship headers, copyright notices, license notices, or attribution comments from original SniffRTP source files.

You may add your own contributor notices below or alongside the existing notices.

## 9. Binary and JAR Redistribution

Redistributing SniffRTP only as a compiled JAR does not remove the attribution requirements.

A redistributed JAR containing SniffRTP code must preserve the required licensing and attribution information included in the distributed package or plugin resources.

A distributor may not intentionally strip attribution resources from a compiled copy in order to conceal the origin of SniffRTP.

## 10. README and Public Distribution Pages

When SniffRTP or a SniffRTP-derived version is publicly redistributed through a repository, plugin marketplace, download page, release page, or similar public distribution page, the distributor must provide reasonably visible attribution stating that the software is based on or derived from SniffRTP by:

(deepslate/sniff/sussy)**imsoback**

This requirement does not require the original author's name to be the largest or most prominent text on the page, but it must not be intentionally hidden.

## 11. Commercial Use

Commercial use is permitted.

You may:

* sell access to servers using SniffRTP;
* include SniffRTP in paid server packages;
* charge for installation or configuration;
* commercially distribute modified versions;
* use SniffRTP in commercial infrastructure.

Commercial use does not grant ownership of the original SniffRTP project and does not remove any attribution requirement.

A seller must not falsely advertise themselves as the original creator of SniffRTP.

## 12. Forks and Derivative Projects

Forks are permitted.

Derivative projects are permitted.

Substantial modifications are permitted.

However, any fork or derivative project containing SniffRTP code must retain the attribution requirements of this License.

A complete rewrite that contains no SniffRTP code and does not copy protectable SniffRTP material is not governed by this License merely because it implements similar functionality.

## 13. No False Endorsement

You may not state or imply that:

* your fork is officially maintained by the original author;
* your modifications were approved by the original author;
* the original author endorses your product, server, company, or service;
* your modified version is an official SniffRTP release;

unless the original author has explicitly authorized such representation.

## 14. Original Project Identity

The name "SniffRTP" may be used when accurately referring to the original project or a fork derived from it.

A distributor must not intentionally use the SniffRTP identity in a deceptive manner intended to make users believe an unofficial modified release came directly from the original author.

## 15. Preservation of Attribution Mechanisms

You may not intentionally modify SniffRTP for the primary purpose of defeating, bypassing, deleting, concealing, or automatically removing the attribution requirements imposed by this License.

Code specifically designed to remove mandatory SniffRTP attribution from redistributed copies is not permitted under this License.

## 16. Compliance Required for Redistribution

If you redistribute SniffRTP or a derivative work, you are responsible for ensuring that your redistributed copy complies with this License.

Receiving SniffRTP from another party without proper attribution does not grant permission to continue distributing a non-compliant copy.

## 17. Termination

Your rights under this License terminate automatically if you materially violate its conditions.

After termination, you must stop distributing SniffRTP and SniffRTP-derived copies unless and until the violation has been corrected and the original author permits continued distribution where legally required.

Rights of users who previously received compliant copies are not automatically terminated solely because a distributor later violates this License.

